-- #567: the wilds' nodes planted only where the walk graph climbs to them.
--
-- #520 found that the slope test the flood and the Flint client's walk graph
-- share (`rules::ground::slope_lets_through`) strode 2 units on gentle ground,
-- and stepped over the face past a valley's floor: the slope kinks there and
-- climbs from about 0.7 past the cliff (1.2) within a unit, where the
-- server's step stops. It now looks again, every 0.25, at any stride whose
-- slope jumps by more than 0.15. The walk graph took it at #520; the flood
-- kept the old test until now, since the reached cells change.
--
-- The tin and the outcrops draw from a different list of reached cells, so
-- every one of them moves, as at #347. Nothing else moves. So this deletes
-- the rows the plan no longer has, by id, and inserts the new ones. Nothing
-- a player owns is a node; a node half gathered starts over.
--
-- The rows come from the ignored test `print_node_replan`, and
-- `the_migration_writes_the_default_plan` checks the plan still matches.
--
-- deleted and inserted, 2389 each, all in the wilderness:
--   rock_outcrop: 1991
--   tin_vein: 398

